      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5995863::chunk::000::abstract::63aa5c975c"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "In the conventional microstructure, the ordered B2 phase forms the continuous matrix.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5995863::chunk::000::abstract::63aa5c975c"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The continuous ordered B2 matrix causes or contributes to poor room-temperature ductility.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5995863::chunk::000::abstract::63aa5c975c"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "An inverted microstructure consists of discrete B2 precipitates dispersed within a continuous BCC matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5995863::chunk::000::abstract::63aa5c975c"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Thermomechanical processing can produce the proposed inverted phase distribution.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Modified alloying can produce the proposed inverted phase distribution.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Discrete B2 precipitates act as effective strengthening agents.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5995863::chunk::000::abstract::63aa5c975c"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preventing the B2 phase from forming a continuous or percolating network reduces its impairment of ductility.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5995863::chunk::000::abstract::63aa5c975c"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "A continuous BCC matrix provides greater plasticity than a continuous B2 matrix.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5995863::chunk::000::abstract::63aa5c975c"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The inverted BCC + B2 microstructure improves room-temperature compressive ductility.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5995863::chunk::000::abstract::63aa5c975c"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The inverted microstructure maintains high yield strength at room temperature.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5995863::chunk::000::abstract::63aa5c975c"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The inverted microstructure maintains high yield strength at elevated temperature.",
